A||N||27||FieroJoe||Paint Finally Done!!! (pics)||||6||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||04-15-2001||09:45 PM||||Ah yes, my car finally is a uniform color now!  I am used to seeing all the different colors of body filler, various primers from previous paint jobs, and the color of the body panels themselves.<P>It took us a about a week and a half of hard work to get it all prepped, and we primed and painted all the way to the base coat last night, and finished up today with the clear.<P>It still needs to be sanded w/1500 and rubbed out and polished, but for now the only thing I have left to paint is the molding that is still on the car (gray primed stuff).  I am doing that tomorrow.<P>here's some pics showing the progress:<P>All sanded and filled:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/frontside_2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rightbackside_1.jpg"> <P>all taped off back in our shop:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/leftfront.jpg"> <P><BR>last night's base coat:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front_7.jpg"> <P>and finally the clear coat!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010001_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010004.jpg"> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000001||grinthock||04-15-2001||09:49 PM||||Looks good so far, did you do that in your garage?  I do'nt know much about paint but i thought you needed a down draft booth||||reg||14
Z||000002||FieroJoe||04-15-2001||10:04 PM||||Yes it was done in our own garage.  No, you dont <I>need</I> a down draft booth and all that, but it does help to keep dust down.  We try our best, but still some dust does get into it.  That is what 1500 grit sandpaper and a DA polisher are for.  We have painted many cars back there and they still have turned out great.  We'd like to have a booth, but we dont have $250,000 to toss around!<P>This was our first car using a HVLP gun too.  It was nice, saved a lot of paint, minimal overspray.  DeVilbiss Millenium GTI, very nice!||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||04-15-2001||10:04 PM||||Beautiful job!  And in my personal opinion, I think that blue is the best looking color on a Fiero!  Amongst a million other plans for my GT, painting it that Fiero blue is one of my future plans.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I don't know how it'll look with the Beechwood interior, but I really don't care!||||reg||14
