Z||000011||FieroJoe||04-16-2001||10:10 AM||||Thanks guys!<P><B>M7F</B>  Yes, I have white face gauges.  Though all the interior is out, I wanted the temp gauge and tach so I could make sure I got the needles all recalibrated, before I put stuff back together<P><B>rogergarrison</B>  Yeah, quite amazing the difference, not too hazy in there!  I was even in there when my dad was spraying it.  He uses a respirator and a hood, while I just had a mask on but it didnt bother me too much.<P><B>bHooper</B>  Yes, it is factory blue.  I love the color!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||04-16-2001||10:44 AM||||It came out great!  Nice job!  I haven't painted anything larger than my spoiler, but I certainly can feel for your troubles in a garage keeping the dust down!  I had the spoiler up in the air about four feet, and still got some dust in it (and a bug!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).  Sanded them out and it looks great.  Are you keeping the moldings black on the car?||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroJoe||04-16-2001||10:46 AM||||Yes, I am painting the moldings black tonight.  The next Fiero I get, if we paint it, I will probably try body color moldings.||||reg||1
