Z||000022||FieroJoe||04-20-2001||10:58 PM||||Cost of the materials was roughly $350.  But some of the stuff we already had, like some reducer and hardender and thinner.<P>We did buy a new gun for this, and it ran $350 also.<P>Our compressor setup prolly is about $700 total, seeing as we had 2 compressors running, the regulator and all the piping and hoses.<P>If you are going to do it one time, and dont plan on painting any other cars, it's really not worth the investment.  Your best bet would be to do all the body work, sanding and prepping yourself, and then take it to a shop to be painted.  You'll save big big bucks there.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Fiero87311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto near completion!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||rogergarrison||04-21-2001||07:40 AM||||If your painting at home, best time is to start spraying early in the morning. Less dust in the air and the bug wont be out till it warms up, never try it at nite there everywhere. Just a neat note: I did a custom paint job once on an older Camaro in laquer. just when i got the final clear coats on with lots of retarder a Monarch butterfly (the brite colored ones about 3 inches across) landed rite on the hood. We were so po's till I had a brainstorm. I just gently pushed it deeper into the finish and cleared the heck out of it. We didnt have time to let it dry and redo it before an indoors car show. After wet sanding and buffing it looked awesome. everyone at show was staring and remarking about the incredible airbrush job. HEHEHE||||reg||1
Z||000024||Spektyr||04-21-2001||07:54 AM||||ROTFLMAO!<P>I can see it now... somewhere someone is reading this and realizing his two hobbies can finally merge into one...<P>Fiero's and... rare butterfly collecting!<P>hehe<P>As for me I think I'll be going with a very dark color, black or red, blue or green so dark that it's nearly black.<P>A Spektyr isn't exactly a bright and cheery thing, after all.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)||||reg||1
